# SPA fallback for static hosts that read Netlify-style _redirects
# (Cloudflare Pages, Netlify). Vercel ignores this file and uses the
# "rewrites" block in vercel.json instead; the two must stay in step.
#
# This exists so the frontend can be served from somewhere other than Vercel
# without a code change. Routing is hand-rolled on the History API (App.tsx),
# so every deep link — /agapps, /admin, /blog/<slug> — arrives at the host as a
# path with no file behind it. Without this rule the host answers 404 and the
# app never boots.
#
# Real files win over this rule on both hosts, which is what the prerendered
# pages depend on: scripts/prerender.mjs writes dist/<route>/index.html for
# every indexable marketing route, and the host serves those directly. Only
# paths with nothing on disk fall through to the noindex shell — the same
# order Vercel applies.
/*  /_fallback.html  200
